WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
It's eight o'clock: «Il est
huit heures.» It's Monday:

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:07.300
«C'est lundi.» English
says 'it is' both times.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.280
French makes a choice.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.660
Now try 'it is hard'.

5
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.590
French has more than one way to say that,

6
00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.840
too. So before you write 'it is hard',

7
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.030
what do you need to know about 'it'?

8
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.900
In this mission, you'll
follow a flowchart from 'it

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.170
is' plus an adjective to the right French.

10
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:30.230
Then you'll build «c'est» and
«il est» sentences from chips.

11
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.590
Your mission: work out what
'it' really is, every time.
